 "title": "CAT811: microprocessor supply supervisor in a 4-pin SOT-143, with manual reset input",
 "source": {
  "document": "CAT811/D",
  "revision": "Rev. 4, May 2024",
  "pages": 10
 },
 "summary": "A voltage supervisor for microprocessor systems in a 4-pin SOT-143. It holds its push-pull, active-low RESET output low whenever VCC is under a factory-set threshold and keeps it low for at least 140 ms once VCC is back above it; a low on the MR input, which has an internal pull-up of about 20 kΩ, forces the same reset. Seven threshold options from 2.32 V to 4.63 V cover 5 V, 3.3 V, 3.0 V and 2.5 V rails, and the output state holds down to VCC = 1.0 V. CAT811TTBI-GT3 is the 3.08 V threshold part. The CAT811 is marked discontinued and not recommended for new designs.",
