   "title": "RESET valid with VCC under 1.0 V",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "The CAT811 watches its own supply. A 100 kΩ resistor from RESET to ground keeps the reset line in a known state when VCC is below 1.0 V; the exact value is not critical. MR comes out to a terminal for an external reset signal.",
