   "title": "Bi-directional reset pin interfacing",
   "page": 7,
   "description": "For a processor whose reset pin is both input and output (a 68HC11, for one), a 4.7 kΩ resistor sits in series between the CAT811 RESET output and the processor's reset pin. A buffer taken from the processor side of the resistor gives a buffered RESET for the rest of the system. The CAT811 and the processor share the supply and ground; MR comes out to a terminal.",
